  "method": [
    "Forty positive and eight NONE tasks were withheld from runtime tuning; the runtime was frozen before measurement.",
    "Each task ran twice in each of four randomized variants. This section displays the two Jev connection lifecycles only.",
    "Actual in-process AdvisorSession.recommend is compared with the same original selector using a fresh HTTPS client for each request.",
    "Session construction, fresh inventory copies, validation, lazy TLS setup, selection and summary are timed; imports and one-time setup are excluded.",
    "Each repetition starts a new session. Its first cold request is included; there is no hidden warm-up or result/index cache.",
    "Exact serialized request bodies, decoded responses, hashes and a durable attempt ledger were checked independently.",
    "Intervals resample entire tasks with both repetitions together, using 10,000 bootstrap draws. P95 uses the nearest-rank method.",
    "Request and response evidence persistence is included in every measured variant."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Results describe selector latency in one test environment, not complete agent-task duration.",
    "Cross-request reuse requires a long-lived owner session; separate CLI processes start cold.",
    "This measurement does not prove a native agent hook, automatic inventory eligibility or automatic tool execution.",
    "Only single-skill and NONE decisions are measured in this holdout; other behaviors have separate validation.",
    "Configured proxy environments use the documented fresh-connection fallback.",
    "Decoded JSON responses were retained; original HTTP response-body bytes were not exposed by the client."
  ]
}
